# November 21, 2026: eastern Schoharie County, New York, first close pass (region mohawk, drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny, which offered Gallupville). The Atlas had only the thin Old Stone Fort pin between
# Howes Cave and the Albany County line. Schoharie village: the Old Stone Fort (full entry, replaces lm-old-stone-fort),
# the 1743 Palatine House, St. Paul's Lutheran church and cemetery, the railroad museum on Depot Lane, the courthouse,
# Lasell Hall, Main Street, the Vroman and Sternbergh houses. Gallupville: the Becker Stone House, the Gallupville House
# and the two churches. Central Bridge: the Westinghouse birthplace. Middleburgh: the Middle Fort site, the Best House
# museum, the post office mural, St. Mark's, the Bellinger-Dutton house, the depot and the Upper Middleburgh Cemetery.
# North Blenheim: Lansing Manor (region scho, like the Blenheim bridge).
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); HMdb marker pages, theoldstonefort.org,
# mohawkvalleymuseums.us, schohariepresbyterian.org, drbesthouse.com, villageofmiddleburgh.com and nypa.gov through
# tools/page.py. National Register forms for this county on NPGallery are one-page placeholders and were not read.
